This is the output for the assertion that corresponds to the comment "@@@ new last index of x is lesser than or equal to old last index of x". This assertion is true if the last index of "x" in the initial list is less than or equal to the last index in the updated list. If this is not the case, then it means that an item was added to the array list at a location such that it now points to the same index location as the existing item "x", which could potentially cause bugs or unexpected behaviors in the code.--------------------Here is the corresponding .NET System.Diagnostics.Debug.Assert csharp code for comments that start with "@@@":

```cs
