Test `PUT_CountContract` just validates count operation which is not part of ArrayList operation, so, it--------------------The first line of the "PUT_RemoveContract" method has a comment starting with "@@@ new last index of x is lesser than or equal to old last index of x". This statement can be expressed as a debug.assert statement in C# as follows:

```cs
Assert.That(New_arrListLastIndexOfX, Is.LessThanOrEqualTo(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX), "The new Last Index of x should be lesser than or equal to the old one");
```

This will check if the current last index of x (New_arrListLastIndexOfX) is less than or equal to the previous last index of x (Old_arrListLastIndexOfX). If this assertion passes, then this means that the removal of element x from the list does not affect its last occurrence and the list maintains its ordering. If the assertion fails, it will indicate that the removal process broke the list's order.--------------------Here is a C# code that utilizes Assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@" within the given C# code:

```cs
﻿using System.Diagnostics;
[...]

[PexMethod]
public void PUT_RemoveContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    arrList.Remove(x);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount - 1);
    Debug.Assert(Old_x == x);
    Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX);
    Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
    Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX);
    Debug.Assert(!New_arrListContainsX);

    Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX <= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
}

```
Note that this code assumes that the `ArrayList` class has been implemented in C# and provides the required functions and properties. Moreover, please ensure to compile and execute the tests with the correct conditions to verify the code's correctness.--------------------Output:

